STORY.scripture({"1 KĔPHA 2:24":{"t":"who Himself bore our sins in His body on the timber, so that we, having died to sins, might live unto righteousness – by whose stripes you were healed.","book":"1 KĔPHA"},"2 DIḆRĔ HAYAMIM 32:2":{"t":"And Ḥizqiyahu saw that Sanḥĕriḇ had come and his face set to fight against Yahrushalayim,","book":"2 DIḆRĔ HAYAMIM"},"2 DIḆRĔ HAYAMIM 32:3":{"t":"and he took counsel with his rulers and mighty men to stop the water from the springs which were outside the city. And they helped him.","book":"2 DIḆRĔ HAYAMIM"},"2 DIḆRĔ HAYAMIM 32:30":{"t":"And Ḥizqiyahu himself had stopped the upper outlet of the waters of Giḥon and directed them to the west side of the City of Dawiḏ. And Ḥizqiyahu prospered in all his work.","book":"2 DIḆRĔ HAYAMIM"},"2 DIḆRĔ HAYAMIM 32:4":{"t":"And many people were gathered and they stopped all the springs and the stream that ran through the land, saying, “Why should the sovereigns of Ashshur come and find much water?”","book":"2 DIḆRĔ HAYAMIM"},"DANI'AL 2:44":{"t":"“And in the days of these sovereigns the Al of the shamayim shall set up a reign which shall never be destroyed, nor the reign pass on to other people – it crushes and puts to an end all these reigns and it shall stand forever.","book":"DANI'AL"},"DANI'AL 8:21":{"t":"“And the male goat is the sovereign of Greece and the large horn between its eyes is the first sovereign.","book":"DANI'AL"},"EZRA 1:1":{"t":"And in the first year of Koresh sovereign of Persia, that the Word of (YAHUAH) HWHY by the mouth of Yahrmeyah might be accomplished, (YAHUAH) HWHY stirred up the ruach of Koresh sovereign of Persia, to proclaim throughout all his reign and also in writing, saying,","book":"EZRA"},"EZRA 3:10":{"t":"And when the builders laid the foundation of the Hĕḵal of (YAHUAH) HWHY,they appointed the kohanim in their robes, with trumpets and the Lĕwites, the sons of Asaph, with cymbals, to praise (YAHUAH) HWHY, after the order of Dawiḏ sovereign of Yasharal.","book":"EZRA"},"EZRA 3:11":{"t":"And they responded by praising and giving thanks to (YAHUAH) HWHY, “For He is good, for His kindness towards Yasharal is forever.” And all the people shouted with a great shout, when they praised (YAHUAH) HWHY, because the foundation of the House of (YAHUAH) HWHY was laid.","book":"EZRA"},"EZRA 3:12":{"t":"And many of the kohanim and Lĕwites and heads of the fathers’ houses, the old men who had seen the first House, wept with a loud voice when the foundation of this House was laid before their eyes and many shouted aloud for joy,","book":"EZRA"},"EZRA 3:13":{"t":"and the people could not distinguish the noise of the shout of joy from the noise of the weeping of the people, for the people shouted with a loud shout and the sound was heard far away.","book":"EZRA"},"GALATIANS 4:4":{"t":"But when the completion of the time came, Aluahim sent forth His Son, born of a woman, born under Torah,","book":"GALATIANS"},"LUKE 10:25":{"t":"And see, a certain one learned in the Torah stood up, trying Him, saying, “Teacher, what shall I do to inherit everlasting life?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:26":{"t":"And He said to him,“What has been written in the Torah? How do you read it?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:27":{"t":"And he answering, said, “ ‘You shall love (YAHUAH) HWHY your Aluahim with all your heart and with all your being and with all your strength and with all your mind,’ and ‘your neighbour as yourself.’ ”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:28":{"t":"And He said to him, “You have answered rightly. Do this and you shall live.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:29":{"t":"But he, wishing to declare himself righteous, said to Yahusha, “And who is my neighbour?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:30":{"t":"And replying, Yahusha said, “A certain man was going down from Yahrushalayim to Yahriḥo and fell among robbers, who, both stripping and beating him, went away, leaving him half dead.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:31":{"t":"“And by a coincidence a certain kohen was going down that way. And when he saw him, he passed by on the other side.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:32":{"t":"“And likewise a Lĕwite also, when he came to the place and seeing, passed by on the other side.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:33":{"t":"“But a certain Shomeronite, journeying, came upon him and when he saw him, he had compassion on him,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:34":{"t":"and he went to him and bandaged his wounds, pouring on oil and wine. And having placed him on his own beast, he brought him to an inn and looked after him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:35":{"t":"“And going out on the next day, he took out two pieces of silver, gave them to the innkeeper and said to him, ‘Look after him and whatever more you spend I shall repay you when I return.’","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:36":{"t":"“Who, then, of these three, do you think, was neighbour to him who fell among the robbers?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 10:37":{"t":"And he said, “He who showed compassion on him.” Then Yahusha said to him, “Go and do likewise.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:1":{"t":"Now all the tax collectors and the sinners were coming to Him to hear Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:10":{"t":"“I say to you, in the same way there is joy in the presence of the mal'akim of Aluahim over one sinner repenting.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:11":{"t":"And He said, “A certain man had two sons,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:12":{"t":"and the younger of them said to his father, ‘Father, give me the portion of goods falling to me.’ And he divided his livelihood between them.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:13":{"t":"“And not many days after, the younger son, having gathered all together, went away to a distant country and there wasted his goods with loose living.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:14":{"t":"“And when he had spent all, there arose a severe scarcity of food throughout that land and he began to be in need.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:15":{"t":"“And he went and joined himself to one of the citizens of that country and he sent him to his fields to feed pigs.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:16":{"t":"“And he was longing to fill his stomach with the pods which the pigs were eating and no one gave to him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:17":{"t":"“But having come to himself, he said, ‘How many of my father’s hired servants have bread enough and to spare and I am perishing with hunger!","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:18-19":{"t":"‘Having risen, I shall go to my father and say to him, “Father, I have sinned against the shamayim and before you, and I am no longer worthy to be called your son. Make me like one of your hired servants.” ’","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:2":{"t":"And the Pharisees and scribes grumbled, saying, “This One receives sinners and eats with them.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:20":{"t":"“And having risen, he went to his father. And while he was still a long way off, his father saw him and was moved with compassion and ran and fell on his neck and kissed him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:21":{"t":"“And the son said to him, ‘Father, I have sinned against the shamayim and before you and I am no longer worthy to be called your son.’","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:22":{"t":"“But the father said to his servants, ‘Bring out the best robe and put it on him and put a ring on his hand and sandals on his feet.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:23":{"t":"‘And bring the fattened calf here and slaughter it and let us eat and rejoice,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:24":{"t":"because this son of mine was dead and is alive again and he was lost and is found.’ And they began to rejoice.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:25":{"t":"“And his older son was in the field and when he came and approached the house, he heard music and dancing.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:26":{"t":"“And having called one of the servants he asked what this meant.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:27":{"t":"“And he said to him, ‘Your brother has come and your father has slaughtered the fattened calf because he received him back in health.’","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:28":{"t":"“And he was wroth and would not go in. So his father came out and pleaded with him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:29":{"t":"“And answering, he said to his father, ‘See, these many years I have been serving you and I have never transgressed a command of yours, but to me you have never given a young goat, so I could rejoice with my friends.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:3":{"t":"And He spoke this parable to them, saying,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:30":{"t":"‘But when this son of yours came, who has devoured your livelihood with whores, you slaughtered the fattened calf for him.’","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:31":{"t":"“Then he said to him, ‘Son, you are always with me and all I have is yours.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:32":{"t":"‘And we had to rejoice and be glad, for your brother was dead and is alive and was lost and is found.’ ”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:4":{"t":"“What man among you, having a hundred sheep and having lost one of them, does not leave the ninety-nine in the wilderness and go after the one which is lost until he finds it?","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:5":{"t":"“And having found it, he lays it on his shoulders, rejoicing.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:6":{"t":"“And having come home, he calls together his friends and neighbours, saying to them, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found my sheep which was lost!’","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:7":{"t":"“I say to you that in the same way there shall be more joy in the shamayim over one sinner repenting, than over ninety-nine righteous ones who need no repentance.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:8":{"t":"“Or what woman, having ten silver coins, if she loses one coin, does not light a lamp and sweep the house and seek diligently til she finds it?","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 15:9":{"t":"“And having found it, she calls friends and neighbours together, saying, ‘Rejoice with me, for I have found the coin which I lost!’","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 17:11":{"t":"And it came to be, as He went to Yahrushalayim, that He passed through the midst of Shomeron and Galil.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 17:12":{"t":"And as He was entering into a certain village, He was met by ten leprous men, who stood at a distance.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 17:13":{"t":"And they lifted up their voices, saying, “Yahusha, Master, have compassion on us!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 17:14":{"t":"And having seen them, He said to them, “Go, show yourselves to the kohanim.” And it came to be, that as they were going, they were cleansed.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 17:15":{"t":"And one of them, when he saw that he was healed, returned, praising Aluahim with a loud voice,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 17:16":{"t":"and he fell down upon his face at His feet, giving thanks to Him. And he was a Shomeronite.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 17:17":{"t":"And Yahusha answering, said, “Were there not ten cleansed? But where are the nine?","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 17:18":{"t":"“Was no one found to return to give praise to Aluahim, except this foreigner?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 17:19":{"t":"And He said to him, “Rise, go your way. Your belief has made you well.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:1":{"t":"And having entered, He was passing through Yahriḥo.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:10":{"t":"“For the Son of Aḏam has come to seek and to save what was lost.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:2":{"t":"And see, a man called Zakkai! He was a chief tax collector and he was rich,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:28":{"t":"And having said this, He went on ahead, going up to Yahrushalayim.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:29":{"t":"And it came to be, when He came near to Bĕyth Phaḡi and Bĕyth Anyah, at the mountain of Olives, that He sent two of His taught ones,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:3":{"t":"and he was seeking to see who Yahusha was, but was unable because of the crowd, for he was small in stature.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:30-31":{"t":"saying, “Go into the village opposite you, in which, as you enter, you shall find a colt tied, on which no one has ever sat. Loosen it and bring it here. “And if anyone asks you, ‘Why do you loosen it?’ thus you shall say to him, ‘Because the Master has need of it.’ ”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:32":{"t":"And those who were sent went away and found it as He had said to them.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:33":{"t":"And as they were loosing the colt, the owners of it said to them,“Why do you loosen the colt?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:34":{"t":"And they said, “The Master needs it.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:35":{"t":"So they brought it to Yahusha. And throwing their garments on the colt, they set Yahusha on it.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:36":{"t":"And as He went, they were spreading their garments on the way.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:37":{"t":"And as He was coming near, already at the descent of the Mount of Olives, the entire crowd of the taught ones began, to praise Aluahim, rejoicing with a loud voice for all the miracles they had seen, saying,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:38":{"t":"“ ‘Baruk is the Sovereign who is coming in the Name of (YAHUAH) HWHY!’ Shalom in shamayim and esteem in the highest!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:39":{"t":"And some of the Pharisees from the crowd, said to Him, “Teacher, rebuke Your taught ones.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:4":{"t":"And having run ahead, he climbed up into a sycamore tree to see Him, because He was about to pass by.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:40":{"t":"But He answering, said to them, “I say to you that if these shall be silent, the stones would cry out.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:41":{"t":"And as He came near, He saw the city and wept over it,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:42":{"t":"saying, “If you only knew even today, the matters for your shalom! But now they are hidden from your eyes.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:43-44":{"t":"“Because days shall come upon you when your enemies shall build a rampart around you and surround you and press you on all sides, and dash you to the ground and your children within you. And they shall not leave in you one stone upon another, because you did not know the time of your visitation.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:5":{"t":"And as Yahusha came to the place, He looked up and saw him and said to him, “Zakkai, hurry and come down, for I have to stay at your house today.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:6":{"t":"And he hurried and came down and received Him, rejoicing.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:7":{"t":"And seeing it, they all grumbled, say ing, “He has gone in to stay with a man who is a sinner.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:8":{"t":"But Zakkai stood up and said to the Master, “Look, Master, I give half of my possessions to the poor. And if I have taken whatever from anyone by false accusation, I repay fourfold.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 19:9":{"t":"And Yahusha said to him, “Today deliverance has come to this house – since he also is a son of Aḇrahim.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:10":{"t":"And the entire crowd of people was praying outside at the hour of incense.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:11":{"t":"And a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY appeared to him, standing on the right side of the mizbe'ach of incense.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:12":{"t":"And when Zaḵaryahu saw him, he was troubled and fear fell upon him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:13":{"t":"But the mal'ak said to him, “Do not be afraid, Zaḵaryahu, for your prayer is heard. And your wife Alisheḇa shall bear you a son and you shall call his name Yahuchanon.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:14":{"t":"“And you shall have joy and gladness and many shall rejoice at his birth.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:15":{"t":"“For he shall be great before (YAHUAH) HWHY and shall drink no wine and strong drink at all. And he shall be filled with the Ruach HaQadash, even from his mother’s womb.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:16":{"t":"“And he shall turn many of the children of Yasharal to (YAHUAH) HWHY their Aluahim.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:17":{"t":"“And he shall go before Him in the ruach and power of Aliyahu, ‘to turn the hearts of the fathers to the children,’ and the disobedient to the insight of the righteous, to make ready a people prepared for (YAHUAH) HWHY.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:18":{"t":"And Zaḵaryahu said to the mal'ak, “By what shall I know this? For I am old and my wife advanced in years.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:19":{"t":"And the mal'ak answering, said to him, “I am Gaḇri’al, who stands in the presence of Aluahim and was sent to speak to you and announce to you this besorah.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:20":{"t":"“But see, you shall be silent and unable to speak until the day this takes place, because you did not believe my words which shall be filled in their appointed time. ”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:21":{"t":"And the people waited for Zaḵaryahu and marvelled at his delay in the Dwelling Place.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:22":{"t":"And when he came out, he was unable to speak to them. And they recognised that he had seen a vision in the Dwelling Place, for he was beckoning to them and remained dumb.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:23":{"t":"And it came to be, as soon as the days of his service were completed, he went away to his house.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:24":{"t":"And after those days his wife Alisheḇa conceived. And she hid herself five months, saying,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:25":{"t":"“(YAHUAH) HWHY has done this for me, in the days when He looked upon me, to take away my reproach among men.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:26":{"t":"And in the sixth month the mal'ak Gaḇri’al was sent by Aluahim to a city of Galil named Natsareth,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:27":{"t":"to a maiden engaged to a man whose name was Yosĕph, of the house of Dawiḏ. And the maiden’s name was Miryam.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:28":{"t":"And the mal'ak, coming to her, said, “Greetings, favoured one, the Master is with you. Baruk are you among women!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:29":{"t":"But she was greatly disturbed at his word and wondered what kind of greeting this was.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:30-33":{"t":"And the mal'ak said to her, “Do not be afraid, Miryam, for you have found chen with Aluahim. “And see, you shall conceive in your womb and shall give birth to a Son and call His Name Yahusha. ”He shall be great and shall be called the Son of the Most High. And (YAHUAH) HWHY Aluahim shall give Him the throne of His father Dawiḏ. “And He shall reign over the house of Ya‛aqoḇ forever and there shall be no end to His reign.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:34":{"t":"And Miryam said to the mal'ak, “How shall this be, since I do not know a man?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:35-37":{"t":"And the mal'ak answering, said to her, “The Ruach HaQadash shall come upon you and the power of the Most High shall overshadow you. And for that reason the Qadash (Set Apart One) born of you shall be called: Son of Aluahim. “And see, Alisheḇa your relative, she has also conceived a son in her old age. And this is now the sixth month to her who was called barren, because with Aluahim no matter shall be impossible.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:38":{"t":"And Miryam said, “See the female servant of (YAHUAH) HWHY! Let it be to me according to your word.” And the mal'ak went away from her.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:39":{"t":"And Miryam arose in those days and went into the hill country with haste, to a city of Yahuḏah,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:40":{"t":"and entered into the house of Zaḵaryahu and greeted Alisheḇa.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:41":{"t":"And it came to be, when Alisheḇa heard the greeting of Miryam, that the baby leaped in her womb. And Alisheḇa was filled with the Ruach HaQadash,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:42":{"t":"and called out with a loud voice and said, “Baruk are you among women and baruk is the fruit of your womb!","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:43":{"t":"“And who am I, that the mother of my Master should come to me?","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:44":{"t":"“For look, when the sound of your greeting came to my ears, the baby in my womb leaped for joy.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:45":{"t":"“Baruk is she who believed, for that which (YAHUAH) HWHY has said to her shall be accomplished!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:46":{"t":"And Miryam said, “My being makes (YAHUAH) HWHY great,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:47":{"t":"and my ruach has rejoiced in Aluahim my Saviour.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:48":{"t":"“Because He looked on the humiliation of His female servant. For look, from now on all generations shall call me baruk.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:49":{"t":"“For He who is mighty has done wonders for me and qadash (Set Apart) is His Name.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:5":{"t":"There was in the days of Herodes, the sovereign of Yahuḏah, a certain kohen named Zaḵaryahu, of the division of Aḇiyah. And his wife was of the daughters of Aharon and her name was Alisheḇa.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:50":{"t":"“And His compassion is from generation to generation, to those who fear Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:51":{"t":"”He did mightily with His arm, He scattered the proud in the thought of their hearts.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:52":{"t":"”He brought down rulers from their thrones and exalted the lowly.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:53":{"t":"”He has filled the hungry with good items and the rich He has sent away empty.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:54":{"t":"”He sustained Yasharal, His servant, in remembrance of His compassion,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:55":{"t":"as He spoke to our fathers, to Aḇrahim and to his seed, forever.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:56":{"t":"And Miryam stayed with her about three months and returned to her home.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:57":{"t":"And the time was filled for Alisheḇa to give birth and she bore a son.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:58":{"t":"And her neighbours and relatives heard how (YAHUAH) HWHY had shown great compassion to her and they rejoiced with her.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:59":{"t":"And it came to be, on the eighth day, that they came to circumcise the child. And they were calling him by the name of his father, Zaḵaryahu.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:6":{"t":"And they were both righteous before Aluahim, blamelessly walking in all the commands and righteousnesses of (YAHUAH) HWHY.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:60":{"t":"And his mother answering, said, “Not so, but he shall be called Yahuchanon.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:61":{"t":"And they said to her, “There is no one among your relatives who is called by this name.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:62":{"t":"Then they motioned to his father, what he would like him to be called.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:63":{"t":"And having asked for a writing tablet, he wrote, saying, “Yahuchanon is his name.” And they all marvelled.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:64":{"t":"And at once his mouth was opened and his tongue loosed and he was speaking, praising Aluahim.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:65":{"t":"And fear came on all those dwelling around them and all these matters were spoken of in all the hill country of Yahuḏah.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:66":{"t":"And all who heard them kept them in their hearts, saying, “What then shall this child be?” And the hand of (YAHUAH) HWHY was with him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:67":{"t":"And Zaḵaryahu, his father, was filled with the Ruach HaQadash and prophesied, saying,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:68":{"t":"“Baruk be (YAHUAH) HWHY Aluahim of Yasharal, for He did look upon and worked redemption for His people,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:69":{"t":"and has raised up a horn of deliverance for us in the house of His servant Dawiḏ,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:7":{"t":"And they had no child, because Alisheḇa was barren and both were advanced in years.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:70":{"t":"as He spoke by the mouth of His qadash (Set Apart) naḇi'im, from of old –","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:71":{"t":"deliverance from our enemies and from the hand of all those hating us,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:72":{"t":"to show compassion toward our fathers and to remember His qadash (Set Apart) berith,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:73":{"t":"an oath which He swore to our father Aḇraham:","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:74":{"t":"to give to us, being delivered from the hand of our enemies, to serve Him without fear,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:75":{"t":"in set-apartness and righteousness before Him all the days of our life.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:76":{"t":"“And you, child, shall be called naḇi of the Most High, for you shall go before the face of (YAHUAH) HWHY to prepare His ways,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:77":{"t":"to give knowledge of deliverance to His people, by the forgiveness of their sins,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:78":{"t":"through the tender compassion of our Aluahim, with which the daybreak from on high has looked upon us,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:79":{"t":"to give light to those who sit in darkness and the shadow of death, to guide our feet into the way of shalom.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:8":{"t":"And it came to be, that while he was serving as kohen before Aluahim in the order of his division,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:80":{"t":"And the child grew and became strong in ruach and was in the deserts until the day of showing himself openly to Yasharal.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:9":{"t":"according to the institute of the kehunnah, he was chosen by lot to burn incense when he went into the Dwelling Place of (YAHUAH) HWHY.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:1":{"t":"And it came to be in those days that a decree went out from Caesar Augustus for all the world to be registered.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:10":{"t":"And the mal'ak said to them, “Do not be afraid, for look, I bring you the besorah of great joy which shall be to all people.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:11":{"t":"“Because there was born to you today in the city of Dawiḏ a Saviour, who is Mashiach, the Master.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:12":{"t":"“And this is the sign to you: You shall find a baby wrapped up, lying in a feeding trough.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:13":{"t":"And suddenly there was with the mal'ak a crowd of the heavenly host praising Aluahim and saying,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:14":{"t":"“Esteem to Aluahim in the highest and on earth shalom among men with whom He is pleased!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:15":{"t":"It came to be, when the mal'akim had gone away from them into the shamayim, that the shepherds said to each other, “Indeed, let us go to Bĕyth Leḥem and see this matter that has taken place, which the Master has made known to us.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:16":{"t":"And they came in haste and found Miryam and Yosĕph and the baby lying in a feeding trough.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:17":{"t":"And having seen, they made known the matter which was spoken to them concerning the child.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:18":{"t":"And all those who heard marvelled at what the shepherds said to them.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:19":{"t":"But Miryam kept all these matters, considering them in her heart.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:2-3":{"t":"This took place as a first registration while Quirinius was governing Syria. And all were going to be registered, each one to his own city.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:20":{"t":"And the shepherds returned, boasting and praising Aluahim for all they had heard and seen, as it was spoken to them.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:22":{"t":"And when the days of her cleansing according to the Torah of Mosheh were completed, they brought Him to Yahrushalayim to present Him to (YAHUAH) HWHY","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:23":{"t":"as it has been written in the Torah of (YAHUAH) HWHY, “Every male who opens the womb shall be called qadash (Set Apart) to","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:24":{"t":"and to give an offering according to what is said in the Torah of (YAHUAH) HWHY, “A pair of turtledoves or two young pigeons.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:25":{"t":"And see, there was a man in Yahrushalayim whose name was Shim‛on and this man was righteous, dedicated and looking for the comforting of Yasharal. And the Ruach HaQadash was upon him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:26":{"t":"And it had been revealed to him by the Ruach HaQadash that he would not see death before he sees the Mashiach of (YAHUAH) HWHY.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:27":{"t":"And he came in the Ruach into the Qodash (Set Apart Place). And as the parents brought in the Child Yahusha, to do for Him according to the usual practice of the Torah,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:28":{"t":"then he took Him up in his arms and baruk Aluahim and said,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:29":{"t":"“Now let Your servant go in shalom, O Master, according to Your word,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:30":{"t":"for my eyes have seen Your deliverance,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:31":{"t":"which You have prepared before the face of all the peoples,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:32":{"t":"a light for the unveiling of the gentiles and the esteem of Your people Yasharal.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:33":{"t":"And Yosĕph and His mother were marvelling at what was said about Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:34":{"t":"And Shim‛on baruk them and said to Miryam His mother, “See, this One is set for a fall and rising of many in Yasharal and for a sign spoken against –","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:35":{"t":"and a sword shall pierce through your own being also – so as to reveal the thoughts of many hearts.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:36":{"t":"And there was Ḥannah, a prophetess, a daughter of Penu’al, of the tribe of Ashĕr. She was advanced in years and had lived with a husband seven years from her maidenhood,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:37":{"t":"and she was a widow of about eighty-four years, who did not leave the Qodash (Set Apart Place), but served Aluahim with fastings and prayers night and day.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:38":{"t":"And she, coming in at that moment, gave thanks to (YAHUAH) HWHY and spoke of Him to all who were waiting for redemption in Yahrushalayim.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:39":{"t":"And when they had accomplished all matters according to the Torah of (YAHUAH) HWHY, they returned to Galil, to their city Natsareth.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:4-5":{"t":"And Yosĕph also went up from Galil, out of the city of Natsareth to Yahuḏah, to the city of Dawiḏ, which is called Bĕyth Leḥem, because he was of the house and lineage of Dawiḏ, to be registered with Miryam, who was engaged to him – being pregnant.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:40":{"t":"And the Child grew and became strong in ruach, being filled with wisdom and the chen of Aluahim was upon Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:41":{"t":"His parents went to Yahrushalayim every year at the Festival of the Pesach.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:42":{"t":"And when He was twelve years old, they went up to Yahrushalayim according to the practice of the festival.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:43":{"t":"When they had accomplished the days, as they returned, but the Child Yahusha stayed behind in Yahrushalayim. And His parents did not know it,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:44":{"t":"but thinking He was in the company, they went a day’s journey and were seeking Him among the relatives and friends.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:45":{"t":"And not having found Him, they returned to Yahrushalayim, seeking Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:46":{"t":"And it came to be, after three days, that they found Him in the Qodash (Set Apart Place), sitting in the midst of the teachers, both listening to them and asking them questions.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:47":{"t":"And all who heard Him were astonished at His understanding and answers.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:48":{"t":"And having seen Him, they were amazed. And His mother said to Him, “Son, why have You done this to us? See, Your father and I have been anxiously seeking You.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:49":{"t":"And He said to them, “Why were you seeking Me? Did you not know that I had to be in the matters of My Father?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:50":{"t":"But they did not understand the word which He spoke to them.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:51":{"t":"And He went down with them and came to Natsareth and was subject to them, but His mother kept all these matters in her heart.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:52":{"t":"And Yahusha increased in wisdom and stature and in chen with Aluahim and men.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:7":{"t":"And she gave birth to her first-born Son and wrapped Him up and laid Him down in a feeding trough, because there was no room for them in a lodging place.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:8":{"t":"And in the same country there were shepherds living out in the fields, keeping watch over their flock by night.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:9":{"t":"And look, a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY stood before them and the esteem of (YAHUAH) HWHY shone around them and they were greatly afraid.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:1-2":{"t":"And in the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, when Pontius Pilate was governor of Yahuḏah and Herodes district ruler of Galil and his brother Philip district ruler of Yahtur and the country of Trachonitis and Lusanias district ruler of Aḇilene, Ḥanan and Qayapha being kohen gadols, the Word of Aluahim came to Yahuchanon the son of Zaḵaryahu in the wilderness.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:10":{"t":"And the crowds asked him, saying, “What, then, shall we do?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:11":{"t":"And answering He said to them, “Let him who has two undergarments share with him who has none and let him who has food do likewise.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:12":{"t":"And tax collectors also came to be immersed and said to him, “Teacher, what shall we do?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:13":{"t":"And he said to them, “Collect no more than what is appointed for you.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:14":{"t":"And soldiers also asked him, saying, “What shall we do?” And he said to them, “Do not intimidate anyone or accuse falsely and be satisfied with your pay.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:15":{"t":"But as the people were in expectation and all were reasoning in their hearts about Yahuchanon,whether he was the Mashiach or not,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:16-17":{"t":"Yahuchanon answered, saying to them all, “I indeed immerse you in water, but One mightier than I is coming, whose sandal straps I am not worthy to loosen. He shall immerse you in the Ruach HaQadash and fire. “His winnowing fork is in His hand and He shall thoroughly cleanse His threshing-floor and gather the wheat into His storehouse, but the chaff He shall burn with unquenchable fire.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 3:18":{"t":"And urging with many other words, he brought the besorah to the people.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:14-15":{"t":"And Yahusha returned in the power of the Ruach to Galil and news of Him went out through all the surrounding country. And He was teaching in their qahalim, being praised by all.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:16":{"t":"And He came to Natsareth, where He had been brought up. And according to His practice, He went into the qahal on the Shabbath day and stood up to read.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:17":{"t":"And the scroll of the naḇi Yahshayahu was handed to Him. And having unrolled the scroll, He found the place where it was written:","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:18-19":{"t":"“The Ruach of (YAHUAH) HWHY is upon Me, because He has anointed Me to bring the Besorah to the poor. He has sent Me to heal the broken-hearted, to proclaim release to the captives and recovery of sight to the blind, to send away crushed ones with a release, to proclaim the acceptable year of (YAHUAH) HWHY.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:18-21":{"t":"“The Ruach of (YAHUAH) HWHY is upon Me, because He has anointed Me to bring the Besorah to the poor. He has sent Me to heal the broken-hearted, to proclaim release to the captives and recovery of sight to the blind, to send away crushed ones with a release, to proclaim the acceptable year of (YAHUAH) HWHY.” And having rolled up the scroll, He gave it back to the attendant and sat down. And the eyes of all in the qahal were fixed upon Him. And He began to say to them, “Today this Scripture has been filled in your hearing.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:20":{"t":"And having rolled up the scroll, He gave it back to the attendant and sat down. And the eyes of all in the qahal were fixed upon Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:21":{"t":"And He began to say to them, “Today this Scripture has been filled in your hearing.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:22":{"t":"And all were bearing witness to Him and marvelled at the pleasant words that came out of His mouth. And they said, “Is this not the son of Yosĕph?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:23":{"t":"And He said to them, “No doubt, you shall say this proverb to Me, ‘Physician, heal yourself! Whatever we have heard being done in Kephar Naḥum, do also here in Your country.’ ”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:24":{"t":"And He said, “Truly, I say to you, no naḇi is accepted in his own country.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:25-26":{"t":"“But truly I say to you, many widows were in Yasharal in the days of Aliyahu, when the shamayim was shut up for three years and six months and there was a great scarcity of food in all the land, and Aliyahu was sent to none of them, but to Tsarephath of Tsiḏon, to a woman, a widow.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:27":{"t":"“And many lepers were in Yasharal in the time of Alisha the naḇi and none of them was cleansed except Na‛aman the Aramean.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:28-29":{"t":"And all those in the qahal, when they heard this, were filled with wrath. And rising up they drove Him out of the city and brought Him to the brow of the hill on which their city was built, in order to throw Him down.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:30":{"t":"But He, passing through the midst of them, went away.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:1":{"t":"And it came to be, while the crowd was pressing upon Him to hear the word of Aluahim, that He stood by the Lake of Gennĕsar,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:10":{"t":"so too were Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuchanon, the sons of Zaḇdai, who were partners with Shim‛on. Then Yahusha said to Shim‛on, “Do not fear, from now on you shall catch men.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:11":{"t":"And having brought the boats to land, they left all and followed Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:2":{"t":"and He saw two boats standing by the lake, but the fishermen had gone from them and were washing their nets.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:3":{"t":"And entering into one of the boats, which belonged to Shim‛on, He asked him to pull away a little from the land. And He sat down and was teaching the crowds from the boat.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:4":{"t":"And when He ceased speaking, He said to Shim‛on, “Pull out into the deep and let down your nets for a catch.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:5":{"t":"And Shim‛on answering, said to Him, “Master, we have toiled all night and caught none but at Your word I shall let down the net.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:6-7":{"t":"And when they did so, they caught a great number of fish and their net was breaking, and they motioned to their partners in the other boat to come and help them. And they came and filled both the boats, so that they were sinking.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:8":{"t":"And when Shim‛on Kĕpha saw it, he fell down at the knees of Yahusha, saying, “Depart from me, for I am a man, a sinner, O Master!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 5:9":{"t":"For astonishment had seized him and all those with him, at the catch of fish which they took,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 6:12":{"t":"And in those days it came to be that He went out to the mountain to pray and was spending the night in prayer to Aluahim.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 6:13":{"t":"And when it became day, He called near His taught ones and chose from them twelve, whom He also named emissaries:","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 6:14":{"t":"Shim‛on whom He also named Kĕpha and his brother Andri, Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuchanon, Philip and Bartholomi,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 6:15":{"t":"Mattithyahu and T’oma, Ya‛aqoḇ the son of Alphai and Shim‛on, the one called the Ardent One,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 6:16":{"t":"Yahuḏah the son of Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuḏah from Qerioth who also became the betrayer.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:30-31":{"t":"And see, two men were talking with Him, who were Mosheh and Aliyahu, who having appeared in esteem, spoke of His death which He was about to complete at Yahrushalayim.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:32":{"t":"But Kĕpha and those with him were heavy with sleep. And having awakened, they saw His esteem and the two men standing with Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:51":{"t":"And it came to be, when the days of His taking up were being completed, He set His face to go to Yahrushalayim,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:52":{"t":"and He sent mal'akim ahead of Him. And they went and entered into a village of the Shomeronites, to prepare for Him.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:53":{"t":"And they did not receive Him because His face was set for the journey to Yahrushalayim.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:54":{"t":"And His taught ones, Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuchanon, seeing it said,“Master, do You wish us to command fire to come down from the shamayim and destroy them, as also Aliyahu did?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:55-56":{"t":"But having turned, He rebuked them and said, “You do not know of what ruach you are, for the Son of Aḏam did not come to destroy men’s lives but to save them.” And they went on to another village.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:57":{"t":"And it came to be, as they journeyed on the way, that someone said to Him, “Master, I shall follow You wherever You go.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:58":{"t":"And Yahusha said to him, “The foxes have holes and the birds of the shamayim nests, but the Son of Aḏam has nowhere to lay His head.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:59":{"t":"And He said to another, “Follow Me,” but he said, “Master, let me first go and bury my father.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:60":{"t":"And Yahusha said to him, “Let the dead bury their own dead, but you go announce the reign of Aluahim.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:61":{"t":"And another also said, “Master, I shall follow You but let me first say good-bye to those in my house.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 9:62":{"t":"But Yahusha said to him, “No one, having put his hand to the plough and looking back, is fit for the reign of Aluahim.”","book":"LUKE"},"MARK 10:13":{"t":"And they were bringing little children for Him to touch them, but the taught ones were rebuking those who were bringing them.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:14":{"t":"And when Yahusha saw it, He was much displeased and said to them, “Let the little children come to Me and do not forbid them, for of such is the reign of Aluahim.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:15":{"t":"“Truly, I say to you, whoever does not receive the reign of Aluahim as a little child, shall certainly not enter into it.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:16":{"t":"And taking them up in His arms, laying His hands on them, He baruk them.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:17":{"t":"And as He was setting out on the way, one came running and knelt before Him and asked Him, “Good Teacher, what shall I do to inherit everlasting life?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:18":{"t":"And Yahusha said to him, “Why do you call Me good? No one is good except One – Aluahim.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:19":{"t":"“You know the commands, ‘Do not commit adultery,’ ‘Do not murder,’ ‘Do not steal,’ ‘Do not bear false witness,’ ‘Do not rob,’ ‘Respect your father and your mother.’ ”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:20":{"t":"And he answering, said to Him, “Teacher, all these I have watched over from my youth.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:21":{"t":"And Yahusha, looking at him, loved him and said to him, “One matter you lack: Go, sell all you possess and give to the poor and you shall have treasure in shamayim. And come, follow Me, taking up the stake.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:22":{"t":"But he, being sad at this word, went away grieved, for he had many possessions.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:23":{"t":"And Yahusha, looking around, said to His taught ones, “How hard it is for those who have riches to enter into the reign of Aluahim!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:24":{"t":"And the taught ones were astonished at His words. And Yahusha responding, said to them again, “Children, how hard it is for those who trust in riches to enter into the reign of Aluahim!","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:25":{"t":"“It is easier for a camel to enter through the eye of a needle than for a rich man to enter into the reign of Aluahim.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:26":{"t":"And they were immeasurably astonished, saying among themselves, “Who then is able to be saved?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:27":{"t":"And looking at them, Yahusha said, “With men it is impossible, but not with Aluahim, for with Aluahim all is possible.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:28":{"t":"And Kĕpha began to say to Him, “See, we have left all and we have followed You.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:29-30":{"t":"Yahusha said, “Truly, I say to you, there is no one who has left house or brothers or sisters or father or mother or wife or children or lands, for the sake of Me and the Besorah, who shall not receive a hundredfold now in this time, houses and brothers and sisters and mothers and children and lands, with persecutions and in the age to come, everlasting life.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:31":{"t":"“But many who are first shall be last, and the last first.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:32":{"t":"And they were on the way, going up to Yahrushalayim and Yahusha was going before them. And they were astonished and those who followed were afraid. And again He took the twelve aside and began to say to them what was about to befall Him:","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:33-34":{"t":"“See, we are going up to Yahrushalayim and the Son of Aḏam shall be delivered to the chief kohanim and to the scribes and they shall condemn Him to death and shall deliver Him to the gentiles, and they shall mock Him and flog Him and spit on Him and kill Him. And the third day He shall rise again.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:35":{"t":"And Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuchanon, the sons of Zaḇdai, came up to Him, saying, “Teacher, we wish that You would do for us whatever we ask.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:36":{"t":"And He said to them, “What do you wish Me to do for you?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:37":{"t":"And they said to Him, “Grant us to be seated in Your esteem, one on Your right hand and the other on Your left.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:38":{"t":"But Yahusha said to them, “You do not know what you ask. Are you able to drink the cup that I drink and be immersed with the immersion that I am immersed with?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:39-40":{"t":"And they said to Him, “We are able.” And Yahusha said to them, “You shall indeed drink the cup that I drink and with the immersion I am immersed with you shall be immersed, but to sit on My right hand and on My left is not Mine to give, but it is for those for whom it has been prepared.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:41":{"t":"And when the ten heard it, they began to be sorely displeased with Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuchanon.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:42":{"t":"And Yahusha, calling them near, said to them, “You know that those who think to rule the gentiles are masters over them and their great ones exercise authority over them.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:43":{"t":"“But it is not so among you, but whoever wishes to become great among you shall be your servant.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:44":{"t":"“And whoever wishes to be first among you, shall be servant of all.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:45":{"t":"“For even the Son of Aḏam did not come to be served, but to serve and to give His life a ransom for many.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:46":{"t":"And they came to Yahriḥo. And as He was leaving Yahriḥo with His taught ones and a large crowd, blind Bartimai, the son of Timai, was sitting by the way begging.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:47":{"t":"And when he heard that it was Yahusha of Natsareth, he began to cry out and to say, “Yahusha, Son of Dawiḏ, have compassion on me!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:48":{"t":"And many were reprimanding him to be silent, but he cried out all the more, “Son of Dawiḏ, have compassion on me!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:49":{"t":"And Yahusha stopped and said, “Call him.” And they called the blind man, saying to him, “Take courage, arise, He is calling you.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:50":{"t":"And he, throwing aside his garment, rose and came to Yahusha.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:51":{"t":"And Yahusha responding, said to him, “What do you desire I do for you?” And the blind man said to Him, “Rabboni, that I receive my sight.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 10:52":{"t":"And Yahusha said to him, “Go, your belief has healed you.” And immediately he saw again and followed Yahusha on the way.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:12":{"t":"And immediately the Ruach drove Him into the wilderness.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:21":{"t":"And they went into Kephar Naḥum and immediately on the Shabbath He went into the qahal and taught.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:22":{"t":"And they were astonished at His teaching, for He was teaching them as possessing authority and not as the scribes.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:23-24":{"t":"And there was a man in their qahal with an unclean ruach and he cried out, saying, “Ha! What have we to do with You, Yahusha of Natsareth? Did You come to destroy us? I know who You are: the Qadash (Set Apart One) of Aluahim!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:25":{"t":"And Yahusha rebuked him, saying, “Be silenced and come out of Him!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:26":{"t":"And throwing him into convulsions, the unclean ruach called out with a loud voice and came out of him.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:27":{"t":"And they were all so amazed, as to reason among themselves, saying, “What is this, a fresh teaching? With authority He commands even the unclean ruchot and they obey Him!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:28":{"t":"And news about Him immediately spread into all the country around Galil.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:29":{"t":"And coming out of the qahal, they went straight to the house of Shim‛on and Andri, with Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuchanon.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:30":{"t":"And the mother-in-law of Shim‛on lay sick with inflammation and immediately they spoke to Him about her.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:31":{"t":"And having come, He took her by the hand and lifted her up and immediately the inflammation left her and she served them.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:32":{"t":"And when evening came, when the sun had set, they brought to Him all who were sick and those who were demon possessed.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:33":{"t":"And the entire city had gathered at the door.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 1:34":{"t":"And He healed many who were sick with various diseases and cast out many demons and was not allowing the demons to speak, because they knew Him.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:1":{"t":"And some days later He again entered into Kephar Naḥum and it was heard that He was in the house.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:10":{"t":"“But in order for you to know that the Son of Aḏam possesses authority on earth to forgive sins...” He said to the paralytic,","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:11":{"t":"“I say to you, rise, take up your bed and go to your house.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:12":{"t":"He rose straightaway, took up the bed and went out before all, so that all were amazed and praised Aluahim, saying, “We have never seen the like of it!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:2":{"t":"And so many gathered together, that there was no more room, not even at the door. And He spoke the Word to them.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:3":{"t":"And they came to Him, bringing a paralytic, carried by four.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:4":{"t":"And not being able to come near Him because of the crowd, they uncovered the roof where He was. And when they had broken through, they let down the bed on which the paralytic was lying.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:5":{"t":"And when Yahusha saw their belief, He said to the paralytic, “Son, your sins are forgiven you.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:6":{"t":"Now some of the scribes were sitting there and reasoning in their hearts,","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:7":{"t":"“Why does this One talk like this? He is blaspheming! Who is able to forgive sins but Aluahim alone?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:8":{"t":"Immediately Yahusha, knowing in His ruach that they were reasoning that way within themselves, said to them, “Why do you reason about all this in your hearts?","book":"MARK"},"MARK 2:9":{"t":"“Which is easier, to say to the paralytic, ‘Your sins are forgiven,’ or to say, ‘Rise, take up your bed and walk’?","book":"MARK"},"MARK 4:35":{"t":"And on the same day, when evening had come, He said to them, “Let us pass over to the other side.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 4:36":{"t":"And having left the crowd, they took Him along in the boat, as He was. And other little boats were also with Him.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 4:37":{"t":"And there came a great windstorm, and the waves beat into the boat, so that it was already being filled.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 4:38":{"t":"And He was in the stern, asleep on a cushion. And they woke Him up and said to Him, “Teacher, is it no concern to You that we perish?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 4:39":{"t":"And having been awakened He rebuked the ruach and said to the sea, “Shalom, be still!” And the ruach ceased and there was a great calm.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 4:40":{"t":"And He said to them, “Why are you so afraid? Have you not yet belief?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 4:41":{"t":"And they feared exceedingly and asked each other, “Who then is this, that even the ruach and the sea obey Him!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:21":{"t":"And when Yahusha had passed over again by boat to the other side, a large crowd assembled to Him and He was by the sea.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:22":{"t":"And see, one of the rulers of the qahal came, Ya’ir by name. And when he saw Him, he fell at His feet,","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:23":{"t":"and begged Him strongly, saying, “My little daughter lies at the point of death. Come, lay Your hands on her to heal her and she shall live.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:24":{"t":"And He went with him. And a large crowd was following Him and they were thronging Him.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:25":{"t":"And a certain woman had a flow of blood for twelve years,","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:26":{"t":"and had suffered much from many physicians, spent all that she had and was no better, but rather became worse.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:27":{"t":"Having heard about Yahusha, she came behind Him in the crowd and touched His garment,","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:28":{"t":"for she said, “If I only touch His garments, I shall be made well.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:29":{"t":"And immediately the fountain of her blood was dried up and she felt in her body that she was healed of the affliction.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:30":{"t":"And immediately Yahusha, knowing in Himself that power had gone out of Him, turned around in the crowd and said, “Who touched My garments?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:31":{"t":"And His taught ones said to Him, “You see the crowd is thronging You and You say, ‘Who touched Me?’ ”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:32":{"t":"And He was looking around to see her who did this.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:33":{"t":"And the woman, fearing and trembling, knowing what was done to her, came and fell down before Him and spoke to Him all the truth.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:34":{"t":"And He said to her, “Daughter, your belief has healed you. Go in shalom and be relieved from your affliction.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:35":{"t":"As He was speaking, they came from the ruler of the qahal’s house, saying to him, “Your daughter is dead. Why trouble the Teacher any further?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:36":{"t":"But having heard the word that was spoken, Yahusha said to the ruler of the qahal, “Do not be afraid – only believe.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:37":{"t":"And He allowed no one to follow Him except Kĕpha and Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuchanon the brother of Ya‛aqoḇ.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:38":{"t":"So they came to the house of the ruler of the qahal and saw a commotion and much weeping and lamenting.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:39":{"t":"And coming in He said to them, “Why make this commotion and weep? The child has not died, but is sleeping.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:40":{"t":"And they were laughing at Him. And when He had put them all out, He took the father and the mother of the child and those who were with Him and went in where the child was lying.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:41":{"t":"And taking the child by the hand He said to her, “Talitha, qumi,” which is translated, “Little girl, I say to you, arise.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:42":{"t":"And immediately the girl rose up and was walking, for she was twelve years old. And they were completely astonished.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 5:43":{"t":"But He ordered them many times that no one should know it and said that she should be given food to eat.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:14":{"t":"And coming to the taught ones, He saw a large crowd around them and scribes disputing with them.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:15":{"t":"And immediately, when all the crowd saw Him, they were greatly astonished and running near, greeted Him.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:16":{"t":"And He asked the scribes, “What are you disputing with them?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:17":{"t":"And one of the crowd answering, said, “Teacher, I brought You my son, who has a dumb ruach.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:18":{"t":"“And wherever he seizes him, he throws him down and he foams at the mouth and gnashes his teeth and he wastes away. And I spoke to Your taught ones, that they should cast him out, but they were not able.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:19":{"t":"And He answered him and said, “O unbelieving generation, how long shall I be with you? How long shall I put up with you? Bring him to Me.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:20":{"t":"So they brought him to Him. And when he saw Him, immediately the ruach threw him into convulsions. And falling on the ground, he rolled about, foaming at the mouth.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:21-22":{"t":"And He asked his father, “How long has he been like this?” And he said, “From childhood, and often he has thrown him both into the fire and into the water to destroy him. But if it is at all possible for You, have compassion on us and help us.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:23":{"t":"And Yahusha said to him, “If you are able to believe, all is possible to him who believes.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:24":{"t":"And immediately the father of the child cried out and said with tears, “I believe Master, help my unbelief!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:25":{"t":"And when Yahusha saw that a crowd came running together, He rebuked the unclean ruach, saying to him, “You deaf and dumb ruach, I order you, come out of him and never again enter into Him!”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:26":{"t":"And crying out and convulsing him much, it came out of him. And he became as one dead, so that many said that he was dead.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:27":{"t":"But Yahusha, taking him by the hand, lifted him up and he arose.","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:28":{"t":"And when He came into a house, His taught ones asked Him separately, “Why were we unable to cast him out?”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:29":{"t":"And He said to them, “It is impossible for this kind to come out except through prayer and fasting.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:30":{"t":"And going from there they passed through Galil. And He did not wish anyone to know,","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:31":{"t":"for He was teaching His taught ones and said to them, “The Son of Aḏam is being delivered into the hands of men and they shall kill Him. And having been killed, He shall rise the third day.”","book":"MARK"},"MARK 9:32":{"t":"But they did not understand the word and they were afraid to ask Him.","book":"MARK"},"MATTITHYAHU 11:2-3":{"t":"And when Yahuchanon had heard in the prison of the works of Mashiach, he sent two of his taught ones and said to Him, “Are You the Coming One or do we look for another?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 11:4-6":{"t":"And Yahusha answering, said to them, “Go, report to Yahuchanon what you hear and see: “Blind receive sight and lame walk, lepers are cleansed and deaf hear, dead are raised up and poor are brought the Besorah. “Baruk is he who does not stumble in Me.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 11:5":{"t":"“Blind receive sight and lame walk, lepers are cleansed and deaf hear, dead are raised up and poor are brought the Besorah.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:1":{"t":"And on that day Yahusha went out of the house and sat by the sea.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:2":{"t":"And large crowds were gathered together to Him, so that He went into a boat and sat down. And all the crowd stood on the beach.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:3":{"t":"And He spoke to them much in parables, saying, “See, the sower went out to sow.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:31":{"t":"Another parable He put before them, saying, “The reign of the shamayim is like a mustard seed, which a man took and sowed in his field,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:32":{"t":"which indeed is less than all the seeds, but when it is grown it is greater than the plants and becomes a tree, so that the birds of the shamayim come and dwell in its branches.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:33":{"t":"Another parable He spoke to them, “The reign of the shamayim is like leaven, which a woman took and hid in three measures of meal until all was leavened.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:34":{"t":"Yahusha said all this to the crowds in parables and He did not speak to them without a parable,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:35":{"t":"so that what was spoken by the naḇi might be filled, saying, “I shall open My mouth in parables, I shall pour forth what has been hidden from the foundation of the world.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:4":{"t":"“And as he sowed, some indeed fell by the wayside and the birds came and devoured them.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:5":{"t":"“And others fell on rocky places, where they did not have much soil and immediately they sprang up, because they had no depth of soil.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:6":{"t":"“But when the sun was up they were scorched and because they had no root they withered.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:7":{"t":"“And others fell among thorns and the thorns came up and choked them.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:8":{"t":"“And others fell on good soil and yielded a crop, some a hundredfold, some sixty, some thirty.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 13:9":{"t":"”He who has ears to hear let him hear!”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:22-23":{"t":"And immediately Yahusha made His taught ones enter into the boat and go before Him to the other side, while He dismissed the crowds. And having dismissed the crowds, He went up to the mountain by Himself to pray. And when evening had come, He was alone there.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:24":{"t":"But the boat was now in the middle of the sea, agitated by the waves, for the ruach was against it.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:25":{"t":"And in the fourth watch of the night Yahusha went to them, walking on the sea.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:26":{"t":"And when the taught ones saw Him walking on the sea, they were troubled, saying, “It is a phantom!” And from fear they cried.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:27":{"t":"But immediately Yahusha spoke to them, saying, “Take courage, it is I, do not be afraid.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:28":{"t":"And Kĕpha answered Him and said, “Master, if it is You, command me to come to You on the water.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:29":{"t":"And He said, “Come.” And when Kĕpha had come down out of the boat, he walked on the water to go to Yahusha.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:30":{"t":"But when he saw that the ruach was strong, he was afraid. And beginning to sink, he cried out, saying, “Master, save me!”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:31":{"t":"And immediately Yahusha stretched out His hand and took hold of him and said to him, “O you of little belief, why did you doubt?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:32":{"t":"And when they came into the boat, the ruach ceased.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 14:33":{"t":"And those in the boat came and did bow to Him, saying, “Truly You are the Son of Aluahim.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:13":{"t":"Now when Yahusha came into the parts of Caesarea Philippi, He asked His taught ones, saying, “Who do men say the Son of Aḏam is?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:14":{"t":"And they said, “Some say Yahuchanon the Immerser and others Aliyahu and others Yahrmeyahu or one of the naḇi'im.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:15":{"t":"He said to them, “And you, who do you say I am?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:16":{"t":"And Shim‛on Kĕpha answering, said, “You are the Mashiach, the Son of the living Aluahim.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:17":{"t":"And Yahusha answering, said to him, “Baruk are you, Shim‛on Bar-Yonah, for flesh and blood has not revealed this to you, but My Father in the shamayim.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:18":{"t":"“And I also say to you that you are Kĕpha and on this rock I shall build My qahal and the gates of the grave shall not overcome it.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:19":{"t":"“And I shall give you the keys of the reign of the shamayim and whatever you bind on earth shall be having been bound in the shamayim and whatever you loosen on earth shall be having been loosened in the shamayim. ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:20":{"t":"Then He warned His taught ones that they should say to no one that He is Yahusha the Mashiach.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:21":{"t":"From that time Yahusha began to show to His taught ones that it was necessary for Him to go to Yahrushalayim and to suffer much from the elders and chief kohanim and scribes and be killed and to be raised again the third day.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:22":{"t":"And Kĕpha took Him aside and began to rebuke Him, saying, “Be kind to Yourself, Master, this shall not be to You!”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:23":{"t":"But He turned and said to Kĕpha, “Get behind Me, Satan! You are a stumbling block to Me, for your thoughts are not those of Aluahim, but those of men.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:24":{"t":"Then Yahusha said to His taught ones, “If anyone wishes to come after Me, let him deny himself and take up his stake and follow Me.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:25":{"t":"“For whoever wishes to save his life shall lose it and whoever loses his life for My sake shall find it.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:26":{"t":"“For what is a man profited if he gains all the world and loses his own life? Or what shall a man give in exchange for his life?","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:27":{"t":"“For the Son of Aḏam is going to come in the esteem of His Father with His mal'akim and then He shall reward each according to his works.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 16:28":{"t":"“Truly, I say to you, there are some standing here who shall not taste death at all until they see the Son of Aḏam coming in His reign:”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:1":{"t":"And after six days Yahusha took Kĕpha and Ya‛aqoḇ and Yahuchanon his brother and brought them up on a high mountain by themselves,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:10":{"t":"And His taught ones asked Him, saying, “Why then do the scribes say that Aliyahu has to come first?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:11":{"t":"And Yahusha answering, said to them, “Aliyahu is indeed coming first and shall restore all matters.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:12":{"t":"“But I say to you that Aliyahu has already come and they did not recognise him but did to him whatever they wished. In this way the Son of Aḏam is also about to suffer by them.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:13":{"t":"Then the taught ones understood that He had spoken to them about Yahuchanon the Immerser.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:2":{"t":"and He was transformed before them and His face shone like the sun and His garments became as white as the light.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:24":{"t":"And when they came into Kephar Naḥum, those who received the tax came to Kĕpha and said, “Does your Teacher not pay the tax?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:25":{"t":"He said, “Yea.” And when he came into the house, Yahusha spoke to him first, saying, “What do you think, Shim‛on? From whom do the sovereigns of the earth take toll or tax, from their own sons or from the strangers?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:26":{"t":"Kĕpha then said to Him, “From the strangers.” Yahusha said to him, “Then the sons are exempt.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:27":{"t":"“But, lest we cause them to stumble, go to the sea, cast in a hook and take the fish that comes up first. And when you have opened its mouth, you shall find a piece of money. Take that and give it to them for Me and you.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:4":{"t":"And Kĕpha answering, said to Yahusha, “Master, it is good for us to be here. If You wish, let us make here three booths: one for You, one for Mosheh and one for Aliyahu.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:5":{"t":"While he was still speaking, see, a bright cloud overshadowed them. And see, a voice came out of the cloud, saying, “This is My Son, the Beloved, in whom I did delight. hear Him!”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:6":{"t":"And when the taught ones heard, they fell on their faces and were much afraid.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:7":{"t":"But Yahusha came near and touched them and said, “Rise and do not be afraid.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:8":{"t":"And having lifted up their eyes, they saw no one but Yahusha only.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 17:9":{"t":"And as they were coming down from the mountain, Yahusha commanded them, saying, “Do not mention the vision to anyone until the Son of Aḏam is raised from the dead.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 18:1":{"t":"At that time the taught ones came to Yahusha, saying, “Who, then, is greatest in the reign of the shamayim?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 18:2":{"t":"And Yahusha called a little child to Him, set him in their midst,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 18:3":{"t":"and said, “Truly, I say to you, unless you turn and become as little children, you shall by no means enter into the reign of the shamayim.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 18:4":{"t":"“Whoever then humbles himself as this little child is the greatest in the reign of the shamayim.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 18:5":{"t":"“And whoever receives one little child like this in My Name receives Me.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 18:6":{"t":"“But whoever causes one of these little ones who believe in Me to stumble, it is better for him that a millstone be hung around his neck and that he be drowned in the depth of the sea.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:18":{"t":"But the birth of Yahusha Mashiach was as follows: After His mother Miryam was engaged to Yosĕph, before they came together, she was found to be pregnant from the Ruach HaQadash.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:19":{"t":"And Yosĕph her husband, being righteous and not wishing to make a show of her, had in mind to put her away secretly.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:20-21":{"t":"But while he thought about this, see, a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY appeared to him in a dream, saying, “Yosĕph, son of Dawiḏ, do not be afraid to take Miryam as your wife, for that which is in her was brought forth from the Ruach HaQadash. “She shall give birth to a Son and you shall call His Name Yahusha for He shall save His people from their sins. ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:22-23":{"t":"And all this came to be in order to fill what was spoken by (YAHUAH) HWHY through the naḇi, saying, “See, a maiden shall conceive and she shall give birth to a Son and they shall call His Name Immanu’al,” which translated, means, “Al with us.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:24":{"t":"And Yosĕph, awaking from his sleep, did as the mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY commanded him and took his wife,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 21:4":{"t":"And all this took place that it might be filled what was spoken by the naḇi, saying,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 21:5":{"t":"“Say to the daughter of Tsiyon, ‘See, your Sovereign is coming to you, meek and sitting on a donkey, even a colt, the foal of a donkey.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:1":{"t":"And Yahusha having been born in Bĕyth Leḥem of Yahuḏah in the days of Herodes the sovereign, see, Magi from the East came to Yahrushalayim,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:10":{"t":"And seeing the star, they rejoiced with exceedingly great joy.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:11":{"t":"And coming into the house, they saw the Child with Miryam His mother and fell down and did reverence to Him and opening their treasures, they presented to Him gifts of gold and frankincense and myrrh.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:12":{"t":"And having been warned in a dream that they should not return to Herodes, they departed for their own country by another way.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:13":{"t":"And when they had left, see, a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY appeared to Yosĕph in a dream, saying, “Arise, take the Child and His mother and flee to Mitsrayim and remain there until I bring you word, for Herodes is about to seek the Child to destroy Him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:14-15":{"t":"And rising up, he took the Child and His mother by night and departed for Mitsrayim, and remained there until the death of Herodes, to fill what was spoken by (YAHUAH) HWHY through the naḇi, saying, “Out of Mitsrayim I have called My Son.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:2":{"t":"saying, “Where is He who has been born Sovereign of the Yahuḏim? For we saw His star in the East and have come to do reverence to Him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:3-4":{"t":"And Herodes the sovereign, having heard, was troubled and all Yahrushalayim with him. And having gathered all the chief kohanim and scribes of the people together, he asked them where the Mashiach was to be born.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:5-6":{"t":"And they said to him, “In Bĕyth Leḥem of Yahuḏah, for thus it has been written by the naḇi, ‘But you, Bĕyth Leḥem, in the land of Yahuḏah, you are by no means least among the rulers of Yahuḏah, for out of you shall come a Ruler who shall shepherd My people Yasharal.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:7":{"t":"Then Herodes, having called the Magi secretly, learned exactly from them what time the star appeared.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:8":{"t":"And having sent them to Bĕyth Leḥem, he said, “Go and search diligently for the Child and when you have found Him, bring back word to me, so that I too might go and do reverence to Him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:9":{"t":"And having heard the sovereign, they went. And see, the star which they had seen in the East went before them, until it came and stood over where the Child was.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:1":{"t":"And in those days Yahuchanon the Immerser came proclaiming in the wilderness of Yahuḏah,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:13":{"t":"Then Yahusha came from Galil to Yahuchanon at the Yardĕn to be immersed by him.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:14":{"t":"But Yahuchanon was hindering Him, saying, “I need to be immersed by You and You come to me?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:15":{"t":"But Yahusha answering, said to him, “Permit it now, for thus it is fitting for us to fill all righteousness.” Then he permitted Him.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:16":{"t":"And having been immersed, Yahusha went up immediately from the water and see, the shamayim were opened and He saw the Ruach of Aluahim descending like a dove and coming upon Him,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:17":{"t":"and see, a voice out of the shamayim, saying, “This is My Son, the Beloved, in whom I did delight.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:2":{"t":"and saying, “Repent, for the reign of the shamayim has come near!”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:3":{"t":"For this is he who was spoken of by the naḇi Yahshayahu, saying, “A voice of one crying in the wilderness, ‘Prepare the way of (YAHUAH) HWHY, make His paths straight.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:4":{"t":"And Yahuchanon had a garment of camel’s hair and a leather girdle around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:5-6":{"t":"Then Yahrushalayim and all Yahuḏah and all the country around the Yardĕn went out to him, and they were immersed by him in the Yardĕn, confessing their sins.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:1":{"t":"Then Yahusha was led up by the Ruach into the wilderness to be tried by the devil.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:10":{"t":"Then Yahusha said to him, “Go, Satan! For it has been written, ‘You shall worship (YAHUAH) HWHY your Aluahim and Him alone you shall serve.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:11":{"t":"Then the devil left Him and see, mal'akim came and attended Him.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:2":{"t":"And after having fasted forty days and forty nights, He was hungry.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:3":{"t":"And the trier came and said to Him, “If You are the Son of Aluahim, command that these stones become bread.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:4":{"t":"But He answering, said, “It has been written, ‘Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that comes from the mouth of (YAHUAH) HWHY.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:5":{"t":"Then the devil took Him up into the qadash (Set Apart) city, set Him on the edge of the Qodash (Set Apart Place),","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:6":{"t":"and said to Him, “If You are the Son of Aluahim, throw Yourself down. For it has been written, ‘He shall command His mal'akim concerning you,’ and ‘In their hands they shall bear you up so that you do not dash your foot against a stone.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:7":{"t":"Yahusha said to him, “It has also been written, ‘You shall not try (YAHUAH) HWHY your Aluahim.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:8":{"t":"Again, the devil took Him up on a very high mountain and showed Him all the reigns of the world and their esteem,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 4:9":{"t":"and said to Him, “All these I shall give You if You fall down and worship me.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 5:1-2":{"t":"But when He saw the crowds, He went up on a mountain and when He was seated His taught ones came to Him. And having opened His mouth, He was teaching them, saying,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 5:11-12":{"t":"“Baruk are you when they reproach and persecute you and falsely say every wicked word against you, for My sake. “Rejoice and be glad, because your reward in the shamayim is great. For in this way they persecuted the naḇi'im who were before you.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 5:3-6":{"t":"“Baruk are the poor in ruach, because theirs is the reign of the shamayim. “Baruk are those who mourn, because they shall be comforted. “Baruk are the meek, because they shall inherit the earth. “Baruk are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness, because they shall be filled.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 5:7-10":{"t":"“Baruk are the compassionate, because they shall obtain compassion. “Baruk are the clean in heart, because they shall see Aluahim. “Baruk are the peacemakers, because they shall be called sons of Aluahim. “Baruk are those persecuted for righteousness’ sake, because theirs is the reign of the shamayim.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 7:28-29":{"t":"And it came to be, when Yahusha had ended these words, that the people were astonished at His teaching, for He was teaching them as one possessing authority and not as the scribes.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:10":{"t":"And when Yahusha heard, He marvelled and said to those who followed, “Truly, I say to you, not even in Yasharal have I found such great belief!","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:11-12":{"t":"“And I say to you that many shall come from east and west and sit down with Aḇrahim and Yahtsḥaq and Ya‛aqoḇ in the reign of the shamayim, but the sons of the reign shall be cast out into outer darkness – there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:13":{"t":"And Yahusha said to the captain, “Go and as you have believed, so let it be done for you.” And his servant was healed that hour.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:5-6":{"t":"And when Yahusha had entered Kephar Naḥum, a captain came to Him, appealing to Him, saying, “Master, my servant is lying in the house paralysed, grievously tortured.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:7":{"t":"And Yahusha said to him, “I shall come and heal him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:8":{"t":"And the captain answering, said, “Master, I am not worthy that You should come under my roof. But only say a word and my servant shall be healed.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 8:9":{"t":"“For I too am a man under authority, having soldiers under me. And I say to this one, ‘Go,’ and he goes and to another, ‘Come,’ and he comes and to my servant, ‘Do this,’ and he does it.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:10":{"t":"And it came to be, as Yahusha sat at the table in the house, that see, many tax collectors and sinners came and sat down with Him and His taught ones.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:11":{"t":"And when the Pharisees saw it, they said to His taught ones, “Why does your Teacher eat with tax collectors and sinners?”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:12":{"t":"And Yahusha hearing this said to them, “Those who are strong have no need of a physician, but those who are sick,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:13":{"t":"“But go and learn what this means, ‘I desire compassion and not offering.’ For I did not come to call the righteous to repentance, but sinners.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:27":{"t":"And as Yahusha passed on from there, two blind men followed Him, crying out and saying, “Son of Dawiḏ, have compassion on us!”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:28":{"t":"And when He came into the house, the blind men came to Him. And Yahusha said to them, “Do you believe that I am able to do this?” They said to Him, “Yea, Master.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:29":{"t":"Then He touched their eyes, saying, “According to your belief let it be to you.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:30":{"t":"And their eyes were opened. And Yahusha strictly ordered them, saying, “See, let no one know.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:31":{"t":"But when they went out, they made Him known in all that land.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 9:9":{"t":"And as Yahusha passed on from there, He saw a man called Mattithyahu sitting at the tax office. And He said to him, “Follow Me.” And he rose and followed Him.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"YAHUCHANON 10:40":{"t":"and went once more to the other side of the Yardĕn to the place where Yahuchanon was immersing at first, and there He stayed.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 10:41":{"t":"And many came to Him and said, “Yahuchanon indeed did no sign, yet all that Yahuchanon said about this Man was true.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 10:42":{"t":"And many believed in Him there.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:1":{"t":"And a certain one was sick, Al‛azar from Bĕyth Anyah, the village of Miryam and her sister Martha.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:17":{"t":"Therefore, when Yahusha arrived, He found that he had already been four days in the tomb.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:18":{"t":"Now Bĕyth Anyah was near Yahrushalayim, about three kilometers away.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:19":{"t":"And many of the Yahuḏim had come to Martha and Miryam, to comfort them concerning their brother.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:20":{"t":"Martha, then, when she heard that Yahusha was coming, met Him, but Miryam was sitting in the house.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:21":{"t":"Martha, then, said to Yahusha, “Master, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:22":{"t":"“But even now I know that whatever You might ask of Aluahim, Aluahim shall give You.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:23":{"t":"Yahusha said to her, “Your brother shall rise again.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:24":{"t":"Martha said to Him, “I know that he shall rise again in the resurrection at the last day.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:25":{"t":"Yahusha said to her, “I am the resurrection and the life. He who believes in Me, though he dies, he shall live.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:26":{"t":"“And everyone that is living and believing in Me shall never die at all. Do you believe this?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:27":{"t":"She said to Him, “Yea, Master, I believe that You are the Mashiach, the Son of Aluahim, who is coming into the world.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:28":{"t":"And having said this she went away and called her sister Miryam secretly, saying, “The Teacher is here and calls you.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:3":{"t":"Therefore the sisters sent to Him, saying, “Master, see, he whom You love is sick,”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:32":{"t":"Miryam, therefore, when she came where Yahusha was, and saw Him, she fell down at His feet, saying to Him, “Master, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:33":{"t":"Yahusha, therefore, when He saw her weeping, and the Yahuḏim who came with her weeping, He groaned in the ruach and was troubled,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:34":{"t":"and said, “Where have you laid him?” They said to Him, “Master, come and see.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:35":{"t":"Yahusha wept.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:36":{"t":"The Yahuḏim therefore said, “See how He loved Him!”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:38":{"t":"Yahusha, therefore, again groaning in Himself, came to the tomb. Now it was a cave, and a stone lay against it.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:39":{"t":"Yahusha said, “Take away the stone.” Martha, the sister of him who had died, said to Him, “Master, already he smells, for it is four days.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:4":{"t":"But when Yahusha heard, He said, “This sickness is not unto death, but for the esteem of Aluahim, so that the Son of Aluahim might be esteemed by it.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:40":{"t":"Yahusha said to her, “Did I not say to you, that if you believe, you shall see the esteem of Aluahim?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:41-42":{"t":"So they took away the stone where the dead man was laid. And Yahusha lifted up His eyes and said, “Father, I thank You that You have heard Me. “And I know that You always hear Me, but because of the crowd standing by I said this, in order that they believe that You sent Me.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:43":{"t":"And when He had said this, He cried with a loud voice, “Al‛azar, come out!”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:44":{"t":"And he who died came out bound feet and hands with wrappings, and his face was wrapped with a cloth. Yahusha said to them, “Loosen him, and let him go.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:45":{"t":"Therefore many of the Yahuḏim who had come to Miryam, and had seen what Yahusha did, believed in Him.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:5":{"t":"Now Yahusha loved Martha and her sister and Al‛azar.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 11:6":{"t":"Therefore, when He heard that he was sick, then indeed He stayed at the place where He was, two more days.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:19":{"t":"Now this was the witness of Yahuchanon when the Yahuḏim sent from Yahrushalayim kohanim and Lĕwites to ask him, “Who are you?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:20":{"t":"And he confessed and did not deny, but confessed, “I am not the Mashiach.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:21":{"t":"And they asked him, “What then, are you Aliyahu?” So he said, “I am not.” “Are you the Naḇi?” And he answered, “No.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:22":{"t":"Therefore they said to him, “Who are you, so that we give an answer to those who sent us? What do you say about yourself?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:23":{"t":"He said, “I am a voice of one crying in the wilderness, ‘Make straight the way of (YAHUAH) HWHY,’ as the naḇi Yahshayahu said.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:24":{"t":"And those sent were of the Pharisees,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:25":{"t":"and they asked him, saying,“Why then do you immerse if you are not the Mashiach, nor Aliyahu, nor the Naḇi?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:26-27":{"t":"Yahuchanon answered them, saying, “I immerse in water, but in your midst stands One whom you do not know, the One coming after me, who has become before me, whose sandal strap I am not worthy to loosen.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:28":{"t":"This took place in Bĕyth Anyah beyond the Yardĕn, where Yahuchanon was immersing.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:29":{"t":"The next day Yahuchanon saw Yahusha coming toward him, and said, “See, the Lamb of Aluahim who takes away the sin of the world!","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:30-31":{"t":"“This is He of whom I said,‘After me comes a Man who has become before me, for He was before me.’ “And I did not know Him, but that He might be revealed to Yasharal, therefore I came immersing in water.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:32-34":{"t":"And Yahuchanon bore witness, saying, “I have seen the Ruach coming down from shamayim like a dove and remain on Him. “And I did not know Him, but He who sent me to immerse in water said to me, ‘Upon whom you see the Ruach coming down and remaining on Him, this is He who immerses in the Ruach HaQadash.’ “And I have seen and have witnessed that this is the Son of Aluahim.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:35":{"t":"Again the following day, Yahuchanon was standing with two of his taught ones,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:36":{"t":"and looking at Yahusha walking, he said, “See the Lamb of Aluahim!”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:37":{"t":"And the two taught ones heard him speaking and they followed Yahusha.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:38":{"t":"And Yahusha turning, and seeing them following, said to them, “What do you seek?” And they said to Him, “Rabbi” (which means Teacher), “where are You staying?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:39":{"t":"He said to them, “Come and see.” They went and saw where He was staying, and remained with Him that day. Now it was about the tenth hour.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:40":{"t":"Andri, the brother of Shim‛on Kĕpha, was one of the two who heard from Yahuchanon, and followed Him.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:41":{"t":"First he found his own brother Shim‛on and said to him, “We have found the Mashiach” (which means the Anointed).","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:42":{"t":"And he brought him to Yahusha. And looking at him, Yahusha said,“You are Shim‛on, the son of Yonah, you shall be called Kĕpha” (which means A Stone).","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:43":{"t":"On the following day Yahusha wished to go to Galil, and He found Philip and said to him,“Follow Me.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:44":{"t":"And Philip was from Bĕyth Tsaiḏa, the city of Andri and Kĕpha.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:45":{"t":"Philip found Nethanĕ’l and said to him, “We have found Him whom Mosheh wrote of in the Torah, and the naḇi'im: Yahusha of Natsareth – the son of Yosĕph.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:46":{"t":"And Nethanĕ’l said to him, “Is it possible for any good matter to come out of Natsareth?” Philip said to him, “Come and see.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:47":{"t":"Yahusha saw Nethanĕ’l coming toward Him, and said of him, “See, truly a Yahsra’Alite, in whom is no deceit!”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:48":{"t":"Nethanĕ’l said to Him, “From where do You know me?” Yahusha answered and said to him, “Before Philip called you, when you were under the fig tree, I saw you.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:49":{"t":"Nethanĕ’l answered and said to Him, “Rabbi, You are the Son of Aluahim! You are the Sovereign of Yasharal!”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:50":{"t":"Yahusha answered and said to him, “Because I said to you, ‘I saw you under the fig tree,’ do you believe? Greater than that you shall see.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 1:51":{"t":"And He said to him, “Truly, truly, I say to you, from now on you shall see the shamayim opened and the mal'akim of Aluahim ascending and descending upon the Son of Aḏam.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:1":{"t":"And on the third day there was a wedding in Qanah of Galil, and the mother of Yahusha was there.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:10":{"t":"and said to him, “Every man at the beginning sets out the good wine and, when they have drunk, then that which is poorer. You have kept the good wine until now.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:11":{"t":"This, the beginning of the signs, Yahusha did in Qanah of Galil, and manifested His esteem. And His taught ones believed in Him.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:2":{"t":"And both Yahusha and His taught ones were invited to the wedding.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:3":{"t":"And when they were short of wine, the mother of Yahusha said to Him, “They have no wine.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:4":{"t":"Yahusha said to her, “Woman, what is that to Me and to you? My hour has not yet come.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:5":{"t":"His mother said to the servants, “Do whatever He says to you.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:6":{"t":"And there were six stone water-jugs standing there, according to the mode of cleansing of the Yahuḏim, each holding two or three measures.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:7":{"t":"Yahusha said to them, “Fill the water-jugs with water.” And they filled them up to the brim.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:8":{"t":"And He said to them,“Now draw out and take it to the master of the feast.” So they took it.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 2:9":{"t":"But when the master of the feast had tasted the water that had become wine, and did not know where it came from – though the servants who had drawn the water knew – the master of the feast called the bridegroom,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:1":{"t":"And there was a man of the Pharisees, Naḵdimon was his name, a ruler of the Yahuḏim.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:10":{"t":"Yahusha answered and said to him, “Are you the teacher of Yasharal, and do not know this?","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:11":{"t":"“Truly, truly, I say to you, We speak what We know and witness what We have seen, and you do not receive Our witness.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:12":{"t":"“If you do not believe when I spoke to you about earthly matters, how are you going to believe when I speak to you about the heavenly matters?","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:13":{"t":"“And no one has gone up into the shamayim except He who came down from the shamayim – the Son of Aḏam.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:14":{"t":"“And as Mosheh lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, even so the Son of Aḏam has to be lifted up,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:15":{"t":"so that whoever is believing in Him should not perish but possess everlasting life.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:16":{"t":"“For Aluahim so loved the world that He gave His only brought-forth Son, so that everyone who believes in Him should not perish but possess everlasting life.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:17":{"t":"“For Aluahim did not send His Son into the world to judge the world, but that the world through Him might be saved.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:18":{"t":"”He who believes in Him is not judged, but he who does not believe is judged already, because he has not believed in the Name of the only brought-forth Son of Aluahim.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:19":{"t":"“And this is the mishpat, that the light has come into the world, and men loved the darkness rather than the light, for their works were wicked.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:2":{"t":"This one came to Yahusha by night and said to Him, “Rabbi, we know that You are a teacher come from Aluahim, for no one is able to do these signs You do if Aluahim is not with him.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:20":{"t":"“For everyone who is practising evil matters hates the light and does not come to the light, lest his works should be exposed.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:21":{"t":"“But the one doing the truth comes to the light, so that his works are clearly seen, that they have been wrought in Aluahim.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:22":{"t":"After this, Yahusha and His taught ones came into the land of Yahuḏah, and He remained there with them, and was immersing.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:23":{"t":"And Yahuchanon was also immersing in Ayin near Salim, because there was plenty of water there. And they were coming and were being immersed,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:24":{"t":"for Yahuchanon had not yet been put into prison.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:25":{"t":"Then a dispute arose between some of Yahuchanon’s taught ones and the Yahuḏim about cleansing,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:26":{"t":"and they came to Yahuchanon and said to him, “Rabbi, He who was with you beyond the Yardĕn, to whom you have witnessed, see, He is immersing, and all are coming to Him!”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:27":{"t":"Yahuchanon answered and said, “No man is able to receive any matter unless it is given to him from the shamayim.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:28":{"t":"“You yourselves are witnesses for me that I said, ‘I am not the Mashiach but I am sent ahead of Him.’","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:29":{"t":"”He that has the bride is the bridegroom, but the friend of the bridegroom, who stands and hears him, rejoices greatly because of the voice of the bridegroom. So this joy of mine is complete.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:3":{"t":"Yahusha answered and said to him, “Truly, truly, I say to you, unless one is born from above, he is unable to see the reign of Aluahim.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:30":{"t":"“It is right for Him to increase, but me to decrease.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:4":{"t":"Naḵdimon said to Him, “How is a man able to be born when he is old? Is he able to enter into his mother’s womb a second time and be born?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:5":{"t":"Yahusha answered, “Truly, truly, I say to you, unless one is born of water and the Ruach, he is unable to enter into the reign of Aluahim.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:6":{"t":"“That which has been born of the flesh is flesh, and that which has been born of the Ruach is ruach.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:7":{"t":"“Do not marvel that I said to you, ‘You have to be born from above.’","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:8":{"t":"“The Ruach breathes where it wishes, and you hear the sound of it, but do not know where it comes from and where it goes. So is everyone who has been born of the Ruach.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 3:9":{"t":"Naḵdimon answered and said to Him, “How is it possible for this to take place?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:1":{"t":"So when the Master knew that the Pharisees had heard that Yahusha made and immersed more taught ones than Yahuchanon –","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:10":{"t":"Yahusha answered and said to her, “If you knew the gift of Aluahim, and who it is who says to you, ‘Give Me to drink,’ you would have asked Him, and He would have given you living water.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:11":{"t":"The woman said to Him, “Master, You have no vessel, and the well is deep. From where, then, do You have living water?","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:12":{"t":"“Are You greater than our father Ya‛aqoḇ, who gave us the well, and drank from it himself, and his sons, and his cattle?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:13":{"t":"Yahusha answered and said to her, “Everyone drinking of this water shall thirst again,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:14":{"t":"but whoever drinks of the water I give him shall certainly never thirst. And the water that I give him shall become in him a fountain of water springing up into everlasting life.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:15":{"t":"The woman said to Him, “Master, give me this water, so that I do not thirst, nor come here to draw.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:16":{"t":"Yahusha said to her, “Go, call your husband, and come here.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:17":{"t":"The woman answered and said, “I have no husband.” Yahusha said to her, “You have well said,‘I have no husband,’","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:18":{"t":"for you have had five husbands, and the one whom you now have is not your husband. What you have said is true.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:19":{"t":"The woman said to Him, “Master, I see that You are a naḇi.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:2":{"t":"although Yahusha Himself did not immerse, but His taught ones –","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:20":{"t":"“Our fathers worshipped on this mountain, but you people say that in Yahrushalayim is the place where one needs to worship.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:21":{"t":"Yahusha said to her, “Woman, believe Me, the hour is coming when you shall neither on this mountain, nor in Yahrushalayim, worship the Father.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:22":{"t":"“You worship what you do not know. We worship what we know, because the deliverance is of the Yahuḏim.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:23":{"t":"“But the hour is coming, and now is, when the true worshippers shall worship the Father in ruach and truth, for the Father also does seek such to worship Him.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:24":{"t":"“Aluahim is Ruach, and those who worship Him need to worship in ruach and truth.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:25":{"t":"The woman said to Him, “I know that Mashiach is coming, the One who is called Anointed. When that One comes, He shall announce to us all.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:26":{"t":"Yahusha said to her, “I who am speaking to you am He.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:27":{"t":"And upon this His taught ones came, and they were marvelling that He was speaking with a woman, however, no one said, “What do You seek?”or, “Why do You speak with her?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:28":{"t":"The woman then left her water-jug, and went away to the city, and said to the men,","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:29":{"t":"”Come, see a Man who told me all that I have done. Is this not the Mashiach?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:3":{"t":"He left Yahuḏah and went away again to Galil.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:30":{"t":"They went out of the city and were coming to Him.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:31":{"t":"But in the meantime His taught ones were asking Him, saying, “Rabbi, eat.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:32":{"t":"And He said to them, “I have food to eat of which you do not know.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:33":{"t":"Then the taught ones said to each other, “Did anyone bring Him food to eat?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:34":{"t":"Yahusha said to them,“My food is to do the desire of Him who sent Me,and to accomplish His work.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:35":{"t":"“Do you not say, ‘There are still four months, and the harvest comes’? See, I say to you, lift up your eyes and see the fields, for they are white for harvest – already!","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:36":{"t":"”He who is reaping receives a reward and gathers fruit for everlasting life, so that both he who is sowing and he who is reaping rejoice together.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:37":{"t":"“For in this the word is true, ‘One sows and another reaps.’","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:38":{"t":"“I sent you to reap that for which you have not laboured. Others have laboured, and you have entered into their labours.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:39":{"t":"And many of the Shomeronites of that city believed in Him because of the word of the woman who witnessed, “He told me all that I have done.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:4":{"t":"And He had to pass through Shomeron.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:40":{"t":"Therefore when the Shomeronites came to Him, they were asking Him to stay with them, and He stayed there two days.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:41":{"t":"And many more believed because of His word.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:42":{"t":"And they said to the woman, “We no longer believe because of what you said, for we ourselves have heard, and we know that this is truly the Mashiach, the Saviour of the world.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:5":{"t":"So He came to a city of Shomeron, called Sheḵem, near the piece of land Ya‛aqoḇ gave to his son Yosĕph.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:6":{"t":"And Ya‛aqoḇ’s fountain was there. So Yahusha, being wearied from the journey, was sitting thus at the fountain. It was about the sixth hour.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:7":{"t":"A woman of Shomeron came to draw water. Yahusha said to her, “Give Me to drink.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:8":{"t":"For His taught ones had gone off into the city to buy food.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 4:9":{"t":"The woman of Shomeron therefore said to Him, “How is it that You, being a Yahuḏite, ask a drink from me, a woman of Shomeron?” For Yahuḏim do not associate with Shomeronites.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:1-2":{"t":"After this Yahusha went away to the other side of the Sea of Galil, that is Lake Kinnereth. And a large crowd was following Him, because they saw His signs which He did on those who were sick.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:10":{"t":"And Yahusha said, “Make the people sit down.” Now there was much grass in the place, and the men, numbering about five thousand, sat down.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:11":{"t":"And Yahusha took the loaves and having given thanks He distributed them to the taught ones and the taught ones to those sitting down. And the same with the fish, as much as they wished.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:12":{"t":"And when they were filled, He said to His taught ones, “Gather the broken pieces that are left over, so that none gets wasted.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:13":{"t":"So they gathered them and filled twelve baskets with broken pieces of the five barley loaves which were left over by those who had eaten.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:14":{"t":"Then the men, having seen the sign that Yahusha did, said, “This is truly the Naḇi who is coming to the world.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:3-4":{"t":"And Yahusha went up on a mountain, and there He sat down with His taught ones. And the Pesach was near, the festival of the Yahuḏim.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:5":{"t":"Then Yahusha, lifting up His eyes and seeing a large crowd coming toward Him, said to Philip, “Where shall we buy bread for them to eat?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:6":{"t":"And this He said, trying him, for He Himself knew what He would do.","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:7":{"t":"Philip answered Him, “Two hundred pieces of silver worth of bread is not sufficient for them, for every one of them to receive a little.”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YAHUCHANON 6:8-9":{"t":"One of His taught ones, Andri, the brother of Shim‛on Kĕpha, said to Him, “Here is a boy who has five barley loaves and two fish, but what are these for so many?”","book":"YAHUCHANON"},"YASHAYAHU 11:1-2":{"t":"And a Rod shall come forth from the stump of Yahshai and a Sprout from his roots shall bear fruit. The Ruach of (YAHUAH) HWHY shall rest upon Him – the Ruach of wisdom and understanding, the Ruach of counsel and might, the Ruach of knowledge and of the fear of (YAHUAH) HWHY,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 1:1":{"t":"The vision of Yahshayahu son of Amots, which he saw concerning Yahuḏah and Yahrushalayim in the days of Uzziyahu, Yotham, Aḥaz, Ḥizqiyahu – sovereigns of Yahuḏah.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 35:5-6":{"t":"Then the eyes of the blind shall be opened and the ears of the deaf be opened. Then the lame shall leap like a deer and the tongue of the dumb sing, because waters shall burst forth in the wilderness and streams in the desert.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 36:1":{"t":"And it came to be in the fourteenth year of Sovereign Ḥizqiyahu that Sanḥĕriḇ sovereign of Ashshur came up against all the walled cities of Yahuḏah and took them.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 36:13":{"t":"And the Raḇshaqĕh stood and called out with a loud voice in the language of Yahuḏah and said, “Hear the words of the great sovereign, the sovereign of Ashshur!","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 36:14":{"t":"“Thus said the sovereign, ‘Do not let Ḥizqiyahu deceive you, for he is unable to deliver you,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 36:15":{"t":"and do not let Ḥizqiyahu make you trust in (YAHUAH) HWHY, saying, “(YAHUAH) HWHY shall certainly deliver us, this city is not given into the hand of the sovereign of Ashshur.” ’","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 36:2":{"t":"And the sovereign of Ashshur sent the Raḇshaqĕh with a great army from Laḵish to Sovereign Ḥizqiyahu at Yahrushalayim. And he stood by the channel of the upper pool, on the highway to the Launderer’s Field.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 36:21":{"t":"But they were silent and answered him not a word, for the command of the sovereign was, “Do not answer him.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 36:22":{"t":"And Alyaqim son of Ḥilqiyahu, who was over the household, Sheḇnah the scribe and Yo’aḥ son of Asaph, the recorder, came to Ḥizqiyahu with their garments torn and they reported to him the words of the Raḇshaqĕh.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 36:3":{"t":"And there came to him Alyaqim son of Ḥilqiyahu, who was over the household and Sheḇnah the scribe and Yo’aḥ son of Asaph, the recorder.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 36:4":{"t":"The Raḇshaqĕh then said to them, “Please say to Ḥizqiyahu, ‘Thus said the great sovereign, the sovereign of Ashshur, “What trust is this in which you trust?","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:1":{"t":"And it came to be, when Sovereign Ḥizqiyahu heard it, that he tore his clothes and covered himself with sackcloth and went into the House of (YAHUAH) HWHY,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:14":{"t":"And Ḥizqiyahu received the letter from the hand of the mal'akim and read it. And Ḥizqiyahu went up to the House of (YAHUAH) HWHY and spread it before (YAHUAH) HWHY.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:15":{"t":"And Ḥizqiyahu prayed to (YAHUAH) HWHY,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:16":{"t":"“O (YAHUAH) HWHY of hosts, Aluahim of Yasharal, the One who dwells between the keruḇim, You are Aluahim, You alone, of all the reigns of the earth. You have made the shamayim and earth.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:20":{"t":"“And now, O (YAHUAH) HWHY our Aluahim, save us from his hand, so that all the reigns of the earth know that You are (YAHUAH) HWHY, You alone.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:21":{"t":"Then Yahshayahu son of Amots sent to Ḥizqiyahu, saying, “Thus said (YAHUAH) HWHY Aluahim of Yasharal, ‘Because you have prayed to Me against Sanḥĕriḇ sovereign of Ashshur,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:33":{"t":"“Therefore thus said (YAHUAH) HWHY concerning the sovereign of Ashshur, ‘He does not come into this city, nor does he shoot an arrow there, nor does he come before it with shield, nor does he build a siege mound against it.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:34":{"t":"‘By the way that he came, by the same he turns back. And into this city he does not come,’ declares (YAHUAH) HWHY.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:35":{"t":"‘And I shall defend this city, to save it for My own sake and for the sake of My servant Dawiḏ.’ ”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:36":{"t":"And a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY went out and killed in the camp of Ashshur one hundred and eighty-five thousand. And they arose early in the morning and saw all of them, dead bodies.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 37:37":{"t":"And Sanḥĕriḇ the sovereign of Ashshur broke camp and went away and turned back and remained at Ninewĕh.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:1":{"t":"In those days Ḥizqiyahu was sick and near death. And Yahshayahu the naḇi, the son of Amots, came to him and said to him, “Thus said (YAHUAH) HWHY, ‘Set your house in order, for you are going to die and not live.’ ”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:2":{"t":"And Ḥizqiyahu turned his face toward the wall and prayed to (YAHUAH) HWHY,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:21":{"t":"For Yahshayahu had said, “Let them take a cake of figs and apply it on the boil, so that he lives.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:22":{"t":"And Ḥizqiyahu asked,“What is the sign that I go up to the House of (YAHUAH) HWHY?”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:3":{"t":"and said, “I pray, O (YAHUAH) HWHY, please remember how I have walked before You in truth and with a perfect heart and have done what is good in Your eyes.” And Ḥizqiyahu wept bitterly.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:4":{"t":"And the Word of (YAHUAH) HWHY came to Yahshayahu, saying,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:5":{"t":"“Go and say to Ḥizqiyahu, ‘Thus said (YAHUAH) HWHY, the Aluahim of Dawiḏ your father, “I have heard your prayer, I have seen your tears. See, I am adding fifteen years to your days.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:6":{"t":"“And out of the hand of the sovereign of Ashshur I shall deliver you and this city and protect this city.” ’","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:7":{"t":"“And this is the sign to you from (YAHUAH) HWHY, that (YAHUAH) HWHY does this word which He has spoken:","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 38:8":{"t":"“See, I am bringing the shadow on the sundial, which has gone down with the sun on the sundial of Aḥaz, ten degrees backward.” And the sun returned ten degrees on the dial by which it had gone down.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 39:1":{"t":"At that time Meroḏaḵ-Balaḏan son of Balaḏan, sovereign of Baḇal (Baḇylon), sent letters and a present to Ḥizqiyahu, for he heard that he had been sick and had recovered.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 39:2":{"t":"And Ḥizqiyahu was pleased with them and showed them the house of his treasures, the silver and gold, the spices and precious ointment and all his armoury and all that was found among his treasures. There was not an object in his house or in all his rule that Ḥizqiyahu did not show them.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 39:3":{"t":"And Yahshayahu the naḇi went to Sovereign Ḥizqiyahu and said to him, “What did these men say and from where did they come to you?” And Ḥizqiyahu said, “They came to me from a distant land, from Baḇal (Baḇylon).”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 39:4":{"t":"And he said, “What have they seen in your house?” And Ḥizqiyahu said, “They have seen all that is in my house; there is not an object among my treasures that I did not show them.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 39:5":{"t":"So Yahshayahu said to Ḥizqiyahu, “Hear the Word of (YAHUAH) HWHY of hosts:","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 39:6":{"t":"‘See, the days are coming when all that is in your house and what your fathers have stored up until this day, shall be taken away to Baḇal (Baḇylon); not a matter shall be left,’ declares (YAHUAH) HWHY.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 39:7":{"t":"‘And they shall take some of your sons who are born to you, whom you bring forth. And they shall be eunuchs in the palace of the sovereign of Baḇal (Baḇylon).’ ”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 39:8":{"t":"And Ḥizqiyahu said to Yahshayahu, “The Word of (YAHUAH) HWHY which you have spoken is good!” And he said, “Because there is shalom and truth in my days.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 40:3":{"t":"The voice of one crying in the wilderness, “Prepare the way of (YAHUAH) HWHY; make straight in the desert a highway for our Aluahim.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 53:3-5":{"t":"despised and rejected by men, a man of pains and knowing sickness. And as one from whom the face is hidden, being despised and we did not consider Him. Truly, He has borne our sicknesses and carried our pains. Yet we reckoned Him stricken, smitten by Aluahim and afflicted. But He was pierced for our transgressions, He was crushed for our crookednesses. The chastisement for our shalom was upon Him and by His stripes we are healed.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 61:1-2":{"t":"The Ruach of the Master (YAHUAH) HWHY is upon Me, because (YAHUAH) HWHY has anointed Me to bring the besorah to the meek. He has sent Me to bind up the broken-hearted, to proclaim release to the captives and the opening of the prison to those who are bound, to proclaim the acceptable year of (YAHUAH) HWHY and the day of vengeance of our Aluahim, to comfort all who mourn,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:1":{"t":"In the year that Sovereign Uzziyahu died, I saw (YAHUAH) HWHY sitting on a throne, high and lifted up and the train of His robe filled the Hĕḵal.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:10":{"t":"“Make the heart of this people fat and their ears heavy and shut their eyes; lest they see with their eyes and hear with their ears and understand with their heart and shall turn and be healed.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:11":{"t":"Then I said, “(YAHUAH) HWHY, until when?” And He answered, “Until the cities are laid waste and without inhabitant and the houses are without a man and the land is laid waste, a ruin,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:12":{"t":"and (YAHUAH) HWHY has removed men far away and the forsaken places be many in the midst of the land.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:13":{"t":"“But still, there is a tenth part in it and it shall again be for a burning, like a terebinth tree and like an oak, whose stump remains when it is cut down. The qadash (Set Apart) seed is its stump!”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:2":{"t":"Above it stood seraphim. Each one had six wings: with two he covered his face, with two he covered his feet and with two he flew.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:3":{"t":"And one cried to another and said, “Qadash (Set Apart), qadash (Set Apart), qadash (Set Apart) is (YAHUAH) HWHY of hosts; all the earth is filled with His esteem!”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:4":{"t":"And the posts of the door were shaken by the voice of him who cried out and the house was filled with smoke.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:5":{"t":"And I said, “Woe to me, for I am undone! Because I am a man of unclean lips and I dwell in the midst of a people of unclean lips – for my eyes have seen the Sovereign, (YAHUAH) HWHY of hosts.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:6":{"t":"And one of the seraphim flew to me, having in his hand a live coal which he had taken with the tongs from the mizbe'ach.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:7":{"t":"And he touched my mouth with it and said, “See, this has touched your lips; your crookedness is taken away and your sin is covered.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:8":{"t":"And I heard the voice of (YAHUAH) HWHY, saying, “Whom do I send and who would go for Us?” And I said, “Here am I! Send me.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:9":{"t":"And He said, “Go and you shall say to this people, ‘Hearing, you hear, but do not understand; and seeing, you see, but do not know.’","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:1":{"t":"And it came to be in the days of Aḥaz son of Yotham, son of Uzziyahu, sovereign of Yahuḏah, that Retsin sovereign of Aram and Peqaḥ son of Remalyahu, sovereign of Yasharal, went up to Yahrushalayim to fight against it, but could not prevail against it.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:10":{"t":"And (YAHUAH) HWHY spoke again to Aḥaz, saying,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:11":{"t":"“Ask a sign for yourself from (YAHUAH) HWHY your Aluahim; make deep the request or make it high.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:12":{"t":"But Aḥaz said, “I do not ask nor try (YAHUAH) HWHY!”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:13":{"t":"And he said, “Hear now, O house of Dawiḏ! Is it not enough that you weary men, that you weary my Aluahim also?","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:14":{"t":"“Therefore (YAHUAH) HWHY Himself gives you a sign: Look, the maiden conceives and gives birth to a Son and shall call His Name Immanu’al.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:2":{"t":"And it was reported to the house of Dawiḏ, saying, “Aram has set up camp in Ephrayim.” And his heart and the heart of his people were moved as the trees of the forest are moved with the ruach.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:3":{"t":"And (YAHUAH) HWHY said to Yahshayahu, “Go out now to meet Aḥaz, you and She’ar-Yashuḇ your son, at the end of the channel of the upper pool, on the highway of the Launderer’s Field,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:4":{"t":"and say to him, ‘Take heed and be calm; do not fear or be faint-hearted for these two stubs of smoking fire brands, for the fierce displeasure of Retsin and Aram and the son of Remalyahu.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 8:16":{"t":"Bind up the witness and seal the Torah among my taught ones.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 8:17":{"t":"And I shall wait on (YAHUAH) HWHY, who hides His face from the house of Ya‛aqoḇ. And I shall look for Him.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 9:6-7":{"t":"For a Child shall be born unto us, a Son shall be given unto us and the rule is on His shoulder. And His Name is called Wonder, Counsellor, Strong Al, Father of Continuity, Prince of Shalom. Of the increase of His rule and shalom there is no end, upon the throne of Dawiḏ and over His reign, to establish it and sustain it with right-ruling and with righteousness from now on, even forever. The ardour of (YAHUAH) HWHY of hosts does this.","book":"YASHAYAHU"}});
